 function referenceHtml(){return `<div class="panel-title"><span>MECHANICS REFERENCE</span><em>CANON · INTERPRETATION · IMPLEMENTATION</em></div><div class="reference-grid"><article class="reference-card"><h3>Canon anchors</h3><p>Human sessions use the Cruxtruder, Totem Lathe, Alchemiter, Kernelsprite, and Cruxite artifact in the entry process. Players have dream selves associated with Prospit or Derse. Lands, Consorts, Denizens, Gates, prototyping, and server/client relationships are concepts represented here.</p></article><article class="reference-card"><h3>Interpretations</h3><p>Class and Aspect descriptions are thematic guides, not exhaustive definitions or personality predictions. Generated Land motifs, quest connections, and Denizen trials are creative interpretations rather than definitive canon mechanics.</p></article><article class="reference-card"><h3>Implementation rules</h3><p>Seeded assignment, difficulty labels, server dependency ordering, seven sequential Gate states, descriptive prototype tags, and estimated meteor countdowns are simulation choices. No combat, economy, real-time countdown, or online multiplayer is implemented.</p></article><article class="reference-card"><h3>Data & validation</h3><p>Session data is stored as JSON. Validation checks player and Land references, seven Gates, and server-before-client entry order. Save stores a local browser copy; Export JSON downloads a portable file.</p><button class="action-button" id="validateSession">Validate current session</button></article></div>`}
